apps/desktop/src/routes/diagnostics/diag.content:
This assertion cannot detect a broken `drainPendingQueue`. The implementation (`diagnostics-model.ts:47-48`) is `return [...queue]`, which returns a *copy* and never clears/drains the input. Since `q` has length 1, both the no-op copy and a real drain return length 1, so this test passes even though nothing is actually drained. If a caller relies on the queue being emptied (as the name implies), the same change can be re-applied on the next drain (double-apply). Assert the source queue is cleared and that returned entries match the queued input, e.g.:
```ts
const drained = drainPendingQueue(q);
expect(q).toHaveLength(0);
expect(drained).toEqual([{ key: "b", scope: "app", value: 1, liveSafe: false }]);
```
